    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d734">

                <pb facs="0789" n="779" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg779"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.515/5–1849: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Peiping</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Clubb</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-18T18:00:00+08:00">May 18, 1949—6 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 18—2:41 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>852. ReContel 835, May 13, second paragraph. French and Dutch Consulates, after
                    initial deposit, were approached by representatives <pb facs="0790" n="780"
                        xml:id="pg780"/> bank who requested deposits be changed their personal
                    names. French Consul<anchor n="89" xml:id="d734-f1"/> complied (he later said he
                    felt he might have complied too hastily). Matter understood still be under
                    negotiation with Dutch who requested written communication setting forth bank’s
                    reasoning.</p>
                <p>Received third paragraph, my letter May 11 was returned today by bank without
                    comment. This office considers it has fulfilled its obligations vis-à-vis bank
                    re new regulations which as stated Conreftel do not contain any provision
                    seemingly applicable official funds.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 852, repeated Nanking 545, OffEmb Canton 120, Shanghai 569.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clubb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d734-f1" n="89" xml:id="d734-f1-content">
                <p>Michel Bréal.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
